/**
\page changeM Change Menu

\anchor idx_Change_Menu_82

![](mchange.png)

The <b>Change Menu</b> has all functions related to modifying objects that exist on the layout drawing.

- <i>Properties</i> \anchor idx_Properties_83  - sets <i>XTrackCAD</i> into <i>Property</i> mode. Whenever an object is clicked on while in this mode, the <b>Properties</b> dialog is opened. This dialog allows direct manipulation of settings such as the objects length, position or orientation. (\ref cmdDescribe).

- <i>Select</i> \anchor idx_Select_84  - sets <i>XTrackCAD</i> into <i>Select</i> mode.  Whenever an object is clicked on while in this mode, this selection state of this object is reversed.  If an object was unselected it becomes selected, and vice versa. To unselect all objects press the ESC key, use <b>Deselect All</b> from the <b>Edit</b> (\ref editM) menu or <b>Deselect All</b> from the <b>Pop-up</b> menu (\ref mouseBcmd). (\ref cmdSelect).

- <i>Move</i> \anchor idx_Move_85  - move selected object(s). (\ref cmdMove).

- <i>Rotate</i> \anchor idx_Rotate_86  - rotate selected object(s). (\ref cmdRotate).

- <i>Flip</i> \anchor idx_Flip_87  - turn selected object(s) over or around. (\ref cmdFlip).

- <i>Loosen Tracks</i> \anchor idx_Loosen_Tracks_88  \anchor idx_Track_Loosen_89  - this command reverses the effect of Connect Two Tracks as applied to sectional track.

- <i>Modify</i> \anchor idx_Modify_90  - modify an existing track, or lines. (\ref cmdModify).

- ![](mjoin.png)

- <b>Join</b> \anchor idx_Join_Lines_91  \anchor idx_Join_Track_92  \anchor idx_Track_Join_93  - connect two separate pieces of track or two lines. This command can be used to move one of the pieces of track to the endpoint of the other or to create a connection by laying a stretch of flex-track. (\ref cmdJoin).

- <i>Connect Two Tracks</i> \anchor idx_Connect_Two_Tracks_94  \anchor idx_Track_Connect_95  - creates a connection between track pieces with an option to slightly move the select piece(s) and the pieces they connect to. (\ref cmdConnect).

- ![](msplit.png)

- <i>Split</i> \anchor idx_Split_96  - the <b>Split</b> commands are used to divide up tracks (\ref cmdSplitTrack) or split draw objects (\ref cmdSplitDraw) or use a second Object to Trim (\ref cmdTrimDraw).
The (\ref cmdSplitTrack) command can be used in one of two ways;

  - split a section of flex-track into two connected pieces at the point where a <i>Left-Click</i> is invoked or;

  - disconnect turnouts or sectional track pieces at their point of connection.

- <i>Move Description</i> \anchor idx_Move_Description_97  - move the endpoint description of a track piece to another location. (\ref cmdMoveLabel).

- <i>Raise/Lower Elevations</i> \anchor idx_Raise_Lower_Elevations_98  - raise or lower elevation of selected tracks. (\ref cmdRaiseElev).

- <i>Elevation</i> \anchor idx_Elevation_99  - define an elevation at specified track location (\ref cmdElevation).

- <i>Profile</i> \anchor idx_Profile_100  - display the elevation profile of a definable stretch of track (\ref cmdProfile).

- <i>Clear Elevations</i> \anchor idx_Clear_Elevations_101  - remove elevation parameters from selected track(s).

- <i>Recompute Elevations</i> \anchor idx_Recompute_Elevations_102  - performs a global re-computation of dynamic elevations. It should not be necessary to issue this command as elevations are recomputed as required.

- <i>Change Scale</i> \anchor idx_Change_Scale_103  - change model scale and/or gauge of layout design. (\ref cmdRescale)

- ![](mconvert.png)

- <i>Convert</i> \anchor idx_Convert_104  - changes flex-tracks (Straight, Curve, Joint, Bezier) into a Smooth Cornu or vice versa. (\ref cmdConvert).

- \subpage cmdRescale
- \subpage clrElev
